const html = `<a class="skip" href="#w-h">Skip to content</a><nav class="wm-nav" aria-label="Site"><a class="wm-home" href="/" aria-label="Home" title="Home"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><path d="M12 2.5v2.5M12 19v2.5M2.5 12H5M19 12h2.5M5.3 5.3l1.8 1.8M16.9 16.9l1.8 1.8M5.3 18.7l1.8-1.8M16.9 7.1l1.8-1.8"/></svg></a></nav><main><header class="ch ch1 top"><div><h1>Watchman</h1><div class="hw"><p class="hw-t"><i>tsopheh</i> <span class="he" lang="he">צֹפֶה</span></p></div></div></header><section class="ch ch2 chw" aria-labelledby="w-h"><div><div class="moon" aria-hidden="true"></div><h2 id="w-h">Tsopheh</h2><div class="grid"><div><blockquote>“So you, son of man: I have made you a watchman for the house of Israel; therefore you shall hear a word from My mouth and warn them for Me.<br><cite>Ezekiel 33:7 · NKJV</cite></blockquote><div class="more sup"><div><cite>Ezekiel 33:6 · NKJV</cite><p>But if the watchman sees the sword coming and does not blow the trumpet, and the people are not warned, and the sword comes and takes any person from among them, he is taken away in his iniquity; but his blood I will require at the watchman’s hand.’</p></div><div><cite>Isaiah 62:6 · NKJV</cite><p>I have set watchmen on your walls, O Jerusalem;<br>They shall never hold their peace day or night.<br>You who make mention of the <span class="sc">Lord</span>, do not keep silent,</p></div><div><cite>Psalm 127:1 · NKJV</cite><p>Unless the <span class="sc">Lord</span> builds the house,<br>They labor in vain who build it;<br>Unless the <span class="sc">Lord</span> guards the city,<br>The watchman stays awake in vain.</p></div></div></div><dl class="lex"><div><dt>Root</dt><dd><i>tsaphah</i> <span lang="he">צָפָה</span> · Strong’s H6822</dd></div><div><dt>Meaning</dt><dd>“properly, to lean forward, i.e. to peer into the distance; by implication, to observe, await”</dd></div><div><dt>The word in the verses below</dt><dd><ul class="use"><li><b>Isaiah 62:6</b> <i>shomrim</i> <span lang="he">שֹׁמְרִים</span>, “watchmen”: a different word, from <i>shamar</i> (H8104, “to guard”), not <i>tsopheh</i>.</li><li><b>Psalm 127:1</b> <i>shomer</i> <span lang="he">שׁוֹמֵר</span>, “the watchman,” and <i>yishmar</i>, “guards”: both from <i>shamar</i> (H8104), not <i>tsopheh</i>.</li><li><b>Nehemiah 4:9</b> <i>mishmar</i> <span lang="he">מִשְׁמָר</span>, “a watch” (H4929, from <i>shamar</i>), not <i>tsopheh</i>. Hebrew numbers this verse 4:3.</li><li><b>Isaiah 5:20</b> No watch word in this verse.</li><li><b>Proverbs 18:17</b> No watch word. “Examines” is <i>chaqar</i> (H2713).</li></ul></dd></div></dl></div><div class="more bot"><div><cite>Nehemiah 4:9 · NKJV</cite><p>Nevertheless we made our prayer to our God, and because of them we set a watch against them day and night.</p></div><div><cite>Isaiah 5:20 · NKJV</cite><p>Woe to those who call evil good, and good evil;<br>Who put darkness for light, and light for darkness;<br>Who put bitter for sweet, and sweet for bitter!</p></div><!-- TBD pick: Proverbs 18:17 (examining a claim before deciding). Swap if preferred. --><div><cite>Proverbs 18:17 · NKJV</cite><p>The first one to plead his cause seems right,<br>Until his neighbor comes and examines him.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="ch ch4" aria-labelledby="choose-h"><div><section class="doors" id="choose"><h2 id="choose-h">Records</h2><p class="doors-intro">Every item links to its primary source.</p><ul class="door-list" role="list"><li><a class="door" href="/watchman/federal/" id="door-federal"><span class="door-t">2024–2028 Federal Government</span><span class="door-d">Executive orders, public laws, budget acts, court rulings.</span><span class="door-go" aria-hidden="true">Enter →</span></a></li><li><a class="door" href="/watchman/california/" id="door-california"><span class="door-t">2011–2027 California Government</span><span class="door-d">Chaptered bills, executive orders, budgets, rulings.</span><span class="door-go" aria-hidden="true">Enter →</span></a></li><li><a class="door" href="/watchman/la/" id="door-la"><span class="door-t">LA City/County 2013–2027</span><span class="door-d">City and county shown separately.</span><span class="door-go" aria-hidden="true">Enter →</span></a></li></ul></section></div></section></main><footer class="credits"><p>Scripture taken from the New King James Version®. Copyright © 1982 by Thomas Nelson. Used by permission. All rights reserved.</p><p>Hebrew: Westminster Leningrad Codex (public domain), shown with vowel points, cantillation omitted. Lexicon: Strong’s Hebrew Dictionary (public domain).</p><p>Photos:</p><ul><li>“Tower of David at night-Full moon” by Yair-haklai, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tower_of_David_at_night-Full_moon.jpg">Wikimedia Commons</a>, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. Resized, cropped, compressed.</li><li>“Jerusalem, walls of Old town (010)” by Juandev, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jerusalem,_walls_of_Old_town_(010).JPG">Wikimedia Commons</a>, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>. Resized, cropped, compressed.</li></ul><p>Typefaces: EB Garamond, Frank Ruhl Libre, Inter (SIL Open Font License). <a href="/">Home</a></p></footer>`;
